# Dynamic element write keeps subtype-aware arithmetic

Verifies a dynamic indexed write followed by a dynamic indexed read keeps the
stored subtype: `3dm` plus `2dm` resolves through the measure rule instead of
plain integer addition, so the result is `5dm` rather than `5`.

>>> source
let sizes: int[] = [10mm, 2cm]
let index = 1
sizes[index] = 3dm
print(sizes[index] + 2dm)

<<< stdout
5dm

<<< stderr
